```

But wait—tile 14 is also zero, so if a race reads stale data from tile 14, it gets 0 either way. I need values in non-adjacent tiles so the stale value differs from the correct one.

```python
def generate_inputs(device):
    x = torch.zeros(128, 512, device=device, dtype=torch.float32)
    x[:, 0:32] = 10000.0  # Tile 0
    x[:, 480:512] = -10000.0  # Tile 15
    return [x]
```

Now if a race occurs in tile 0, the stale value is 0 (no previous tile). If it occurs in tile 15, the stale value is from tile 14 which is also 0. Any race would read 0 instead of the large values, making the error obvious. I'll use ±50000 to make the difference even more pronounced.

